// CODATA 2022 recommended values of the fundamental physical constants,
// from the NIST wall chart (NIST SP 961, May 2024):
// https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/pdf/wall_2022.pdf
//
// Each value is a Quantity with its standard uncertainty in the last digits,
// `6.674_30(15)e-11m^3.kg^-1.s^-2`. The seven constants that define the SI
// are exact and carry none. The Checks sheet reproduces some of the derived
// constants from the exact ones, to see that they agree with the chart.

sheet Constants

Value : Quantity[; _.10s]

| Name                                       | Symbol  | Value                          | Kind     |
| ------------------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------ | -------- |
| speed of light in vacuum                   | c       | 299_792_458m.s^-1              | exact    |
| Planck constant                            | h       | 6.626_070_15e-34J.s            | exact    |
| elementary charge                          | e       | 1.602_176_634e-19C             | exact    |
| Boltzmann constant                         | k       | 1.380_649e-23J.K^-1            | exact    |
| Avogadro constant                          | NA      | 6.022_140_76e23mol^-1          | exact    |
| Newtonian constant of gravitation          | G       | 6.674_30(15)e-11m^3.kg^-1.s^-2 | measured |
| vacuum magnetic permeability               | mu0     | 1.256_637_061_27(20)e-6N.A^-2  | measured |
| vacuum electric permittivity               | eps0    | 8.854_187_8188(14)e-12F.m^-1   | measured |
| Bohr magneton                              | muB     | 9.274_010_0657(29)e-24J.T^-1   | measured |
| nuclear magneton                           | muN     | 5.050_783_7393(16)e-27J.T^-1   | measured |
| Rydberg constant                           | Rinf    | 10_973_731.568_157(12)m^-1     | measured |
| Bohr radius                                | a0      | 5.291_772_105_44(82)e-11m      | measured |
| Hartree energy                             | Eh      | 4.359_744_722_2060(48)e-18J    | measured |
| electron mass                              | me      | 9.109_383_7139(28)e-31kg       | measured |
| proton mass                                | mp      | 1.672_621_925_95(52)e-27kg     | measured |
| neutron mass                               | mn      | 1.674_927_500_56(85)e-27kg     | measured |
| atomic mass constant                       | mu      | 1.660_539_068_92(52)e-27kg     | measured |
| classical electron radius                  | re      | 2.817_940_3205(13)e-15m        | measured |
| Compton wavelength                         | lamC    | 2.426_310_235_38(76)e-12m      | measured |
| Thomson cross section                      | sigmae  | 6.652_458_7051(62)e-29m^2      | measured |
| electron magnetic moment                   | mue     | -9.284_764_6917(29)e-24J.T^-1  | measured |
| proton magnetic moment                     | mup     | 1.410_606_795_45(60)e-26J.T^-1 | measured |
| proton gyromagnetic ratio                  | gammap  | 2.675_221_8708(11)e8s^-1.T^-1  | measured |
| fine-structure constant                    | alpha   | 7.297_352_5643(11)e-3          | measured |
| inverse fine-structure constant            | alpha⁻¹ | 137.035_999_177(21)            | measured |
| proton-electron mass ratio                 | mp/me   | 1836.152_673_426(32)           | measured |
| muon-electron mass ratio                   | mmu/me  | 206.768_2827(46)               | measured |
| neutron-proton mass ratio                  | mn/mp   | 1.001_378_419_46(40)           | measured |
| deuteron-proton mass ratio                 | md/mp   | 1.999_007_501_2699(84)         | measured |
| electron g-factor                          | ge      | -2.002_319_304_360_92(36)      | measured |
| electron magnetic moment anomaly           | ae      | 1.159_652_180_46(18)e-3        | measured |
| muon magnetic moment anomaly               | amu     | 1.165_920_62(41)e-3            | measured |
| proton magnetic moment to nuclear magneton | mup/muN | 2.792_847_344_63(82)           | measured |

// Derived constants worked out from the exact ones, set beside the
// published values, which the chart prints to ten digits or so. The format
// `[; .9s]` names no unit, so each value keeps its own, and shows nine
// significant digits since an exact value has no uncertainty to set them. `Agrees`
// holds when the two differ by less than one part in 10^8.
const c  = Constants[Value; Symbol == 'c'].first()
const h  = Constants[Value; Symbol == 'h'].first()
const e  = Constants[Value; Symbol == 'e'].first()
const k  = Constants[Value; Symbol == 'k'].first()
const NA = Constants[Value; Symbol == 'NA'].first()

sheet Checks

Derived   : Quantity[; .9s]
Published : Quantity[; .9s]

| Name                    | Derived          | Published                  | Agrees |
| ----------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------- | ------ |
| Reduced Planck constant | = h / (2 * pi) | 1.054_571_817e-34J.s       | *      |
| Magnetic flux quantum   | = h / (2 * e)    | 2.067_833_848e-15Wb        | *      |
| Faraday constant        | = NA * e         | 96_485.332_12C.mol^-1      | *      |
| Molar gas constant      | = NA * k         | 8.314_462_618J.mol^-1.K^-1 | *      |

Agrees := abs(Derived / Published - 1) < 1e-8
